AC1 scenario -- existing query string:
URL: /subscription-success?flag=success&&flag=failed&&token=c29tZXRva2Vu
parse_str result:
Array
(
    [flag] => failed
    [token] => c29tZXRva2Vu
)
flag === payment_flag (server value)? YES
mangled ?flag key present? NO (good)

AC2 scenario -- no existing query string:
URL: /subscription-success?flag=failed&&token=c29tZXRva2Vu
Matches unchanged "?flag=...&&token=..." shape? YES

Regression-candidate (fragment) probe -- pre-existing on base branch too:
URL: /wallet#evil-fragment?flag=failed&&token=abc123
Array
(
    [path] => /wallet
    [fragment] => evil-fragment?flag=failed&&token=abc123
)
flag/token land inside the fragment, not the query string -- reproduces identically pre-fix (CallbackUrlValidator.php byte-identical to base, and base Processor.php also hardcoded a bare "?" here).
